A||||2||Terrybogin||Do bigger Throttle Bodies improve performance?||||1||
Z||000000||Terrybogin||06-19-2000||10:08 PM||||I have seen Fiero throttle bodies that have been bored to a larger size. Is there a difference in power from this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-19-2000||10:40 PM||||Mine is bored out 3mm. (about 1/6 of an inch)<BR>I haven't dyno'd my car yet, I just used a rough 0-60 time check. HP increase is estimated about 5hp. You can feel the difference over 2000 rpm. The car seems to breathe better mid to high rpm. The set-up also included porting the intake to the larger bore throttle body. I bought mine at the Fiero Store for $199.00. I don't know how much it would cost to have a machine shop do it for you. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||06-19-2000||11:04 PM||||My throttle body is bored out together with the intake runners both upper and lower. I found that the car has much better top end than before.  Did not notice a lot of bottom end power change.  I found that I can easily do 140 mph and the RPM is only about 5000 with another 1000 rpm to go. I could never do that with my stock engine.  <P>Cheers||||reg||1
